Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Alex Deucher <alexander.deucher@amd.com>

Here is the root cause:
The bug arises from enabling Latency Tolerance Reporting (LTR) in an endpoint without confirming that the Root Complex and all intermediate switches support it, as mandated by the PCIe Base Specification. This oversight can lead to Unsupported Request errors during Active State Power Management (ASPM) enablement, as the system attempts to use LTR in an unsupported configuration.

